---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Navigation from '../../components/Navigation.astro';
import PageHero from '../../components/sections/PageHero.astro';
import FAQSection from '../../components/sections/FAQSection.astro';
import FinalCTA from '../../components/FinalCTA.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="AI Architecture for GDPR and EU AI Act Requirements | Ironum"
  description="How Ironum builds AI setups for GDPR and EU AI Act requirements and for customer security reviews: data location, encryption, audit logging, DPA and NDA."
>
  <Navigation />

  <PageHero
    eyebrow="COMPLIANCE"
    title="Built for GDPR and EU AI Act Requirements"
    subtitle="Data protection is not an afterthought. We design every Ironum deployment around it from the start, with European data sovereignty by design."
  />

  <!-- GDPR Compliance -->
  <section class="px-4 md:px-20 py-20 md:py-32">
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto space-y-8">
      <span class="text-orange-500 font-semibold tracking-[0.2em] text-sm uppercase block">GDPR</span>
      <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-5xl xl:text-7xl font-bold">GDPR Requirements in Every Layer</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-500 text-lg font-semibold max-w-3xl">The General Data Protection Regulation requires that personal data is processed lawfully, transparently, and with purpose limitation. We design every AI deployment with these requirements in mind. Meeting them for your processing stays your responsibility as the controller.</p>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 pt-8">
        <div class="border-2 border-gray-100 rounded-2xl p-6 md:p-8">
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-3">Data Residency</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-500 text-lg font-semibold">Our managed setups process and store data in the European Union. Our primary infrastructure runs on Hetzner data centers in Germany (Nuremberg and Falkenstein). If you choose a non-EU service, such as a commercial model API, we document where the data goes.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="border-2 border-gray-100 rounded-2xl p-6 md:p-8">
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-3">Encryption</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-500 text-lg font-semibold">Our setups encrypt data in transit (TLS) and at rest. Key management is agreed per deployment, including keys held in your own infrastructure.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="border-2 border-gray-100 rounded-2xl p-6 md:p-8">
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-3">Audit Logging</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-500 text-lg font-semibold">Our setups can log data access, model queries, and system changes with timestamps, user identity, and action type. Logs can be stored tamper-evident and exported for audits.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="border-2 border-gray-100 rounded-2xl p-6 md:p-8">
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-3">DPA & NDA Included</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-500 text-lg font-semibold">Every Ironum engagement includes a Data Processing Agreement (DPA) under Art. 28 GDPR and a mutual Non-Disclosure Agreement as standard documents.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- EU AI Act -->
  <section class="px-4 md:px-20 py-20 md:py-32 bg-black text-white">
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto space-y-8">
      <span class="text-orange-500 font-semibold tracking-[0.2em] text-sm uppercase block">EU AI ACT</span>
      <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-5xl xl:text-7xl font-bold">EU AI Act: The Timeline That Matters</h2>
      <p class="text-white/70 text-lg font-semibold max-w-3xl">The EU describes the AI Act as the first comprehensive AI law worldwide. For the most serious violations, fines can reach EUR 35 million or 7% of worldwide annual turnover. Here is the timeline.</p>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-6 pt-8">
        <div class="border-2 border-white/10 rounded-2xl p-6 md:p-8">
          <span class="text-blue-400 text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-wider">FEBRUARY 2025</span>
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mt-2 mb-3">Prohibited Practices Ban</h3>
          <p class="text-white/70 text-lg font-semibold">AI systems that manipulate behavior, exploit vulnerabilities, or enable social scoring are banned. We do not build systems for prohibited practices.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="border-2 border-white/10 rounded-2xl p-6 md:p-8">
          <span class="text-blue-400 text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-wider">AUGUST 2025</span>
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mt-2 mb-3">GPAI Model Rules</h3>
          <p class="text-white/70 text-lg font-semibold">Providers of general-purpose AI models must meet transparency requirements, including technical documentation and copyright rules. These duties sit with the model providers; our orchestration layer lets you choose and document which models you use.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="border-2 border-white/10 rounded-2xl p-6 md:p-8">
          <span class="text-blue-400 text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-wider">DECEMBER 2027 / AUGUST 2028</span>
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mt-2 mb-3">High-Risk Rules</h3>
          <p class="text-white/70 text-lg font-semibold">Originally due in August 2026, moved by the Digital Omnibus: stand-alone high-risk systems (Annex III) from 2 December 2027, AI in regulated products (Annex I) from 2 August 2028. Risk management, human oversight and registration in the EU database apply then.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="border-2 border-white/10 rounded-2xl p-6 md:p-8 mt-4">
        <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-3">What This Means for Your AI Deployments</h3>
        <p class="text-white/70 text-lg font-semibold mb-4">If you use AI for hiring, credit scoring, healthcare triage, or other high-risk applications, you need documented risk assessments, human oversight mechanisms, and auditable decision logs. Our setups can include the technical parts of these; whether your system is high-risk is a legal question for your advisers.</p>
        <ul class="space-y-2 text-white/70 text-lg font-semibold">
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-blue-400 mt-1 shrink-0" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7"/></svg>
            Risk classification and impact assessments
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-blue-400 mt-1 shrink-0" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7"/></svg>
            Human-in-the-loop review workflows
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-blue-400 mt-1 shrink-0" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7"/></svg>
            Transparent model documentation
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-blue-400 mt-1 shrink-0" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7"/></svg>
            Audit trails for AI-assisted decisions
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Data Sovereignty -->
  <section class="px-4 md:px-20 py-20 md:py-32">
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto space-y-8">
      <span class="text-orange-500 font-semibold tracking-[0.2em] text-sm uppercase block">DATA SOVEREIGNTY</span>
      <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-5xl xl:text-7xl font-bold">Your Data Can Stay in Europe</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-500 text-lg font-semibold max-w-3xl">European data sovereignty means your data is stored and processed under EU law, with providers you choose. With European operators or your own servers, there is no US parent company that can be subject to US access requests, and no transatlantic transfer is needed.</p>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4 gap-6 pt-8">
        <div class="border-2 border-gray-100 rounded-2xl p-6 text-center">
          <span class="text-blue-600 text-4xl font-bold block mb-2">Hetzner</span>
          <p class="text-gray-500 font-semibold">German hosting provider. Data centers in Nuremberg and Falkenstein, which Hetzner states are ISO 27001 certified.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="border-2 border-gray-100 rounded-2xl p-6 text-center">
          <span class="text-blue-600 text-4xl font-bold block mb-2">Azure EU</span>
          <p class="text-gray-500 font-semibold">Microsoft Azure EU regions for LLM inference in the EU, under Microsoft's DPA.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="border-2 border-gray-100 rounded-2xl p-6 text-center">
          <span class="text-blue-600 text-4xl font-bold block mb-2">On-Prem</span>
          <p class="text-gray-500 font-semibold">Deploy on your own hardware. With open-source models, no external AI API is needed. Air-gapped setups possible.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="border-2 border-gray-100 rounded-2xl p-6 text-center">
          <span class="text-blue-600 text-4xl font-bold block mb-2">RBAC</span>
          <p class="text-gray-500 font-semibold">Role-based access control. Granular permissions. Set up with least privilege.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Audit & Access Control -->
  <section class="px-4 md:px-20 py-20 md:py-32 bg-gray-50">
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto space-y-8">
      <span class="text-orange-500 font-semibold tracking-[0.2em] text-sm uppercase block">SECURITY</span>
      <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-5xl xl:text-7xl font-bold">Audit Logging & Access Control</h2>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 pt-8">
        <div class="border-2 border-gray-100 rounded-2xl p-6 md:p-8 bg-white">
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-3">Audit Logs</h3>
          <ul class="space-y-3 text-gray-500 text-lg font-semibold">
            <li>Queries, responses, and data access can be logged</li>
            <li>Tamper-evident log storage</li>
            <li>Export logs for regulatory audits (JSON, CSV)</li>
            <li>Configurable retention periods</li>
            <li>Alerting on unusual access patterns</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="border-2 border-gray-100 rounded-2xl p-6 md:p-8 bg-white">
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-3">Role-Based Access Control</h3>
          <ul class="space-y-3 text-gray-500 text-lg font-semibold">
            <li>Granular permissions per user, team, and resource</li>
            <li>SSO integration (Azure AD, SAML, OIDC)</li>
            <li>Multi-factor authentication support</li>
            <li>Least-privilege setup with explicit grants</li>
            <li>API key management with scoped access</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <FAQSection items={[
    { question: "How does Ironum support GDPR requirements?", answer: "We provide Data Processing Agreements (DPA) under Art. 28 GDPR, host managed setups in the EU, encrypt data in transit and at rest, and set up audit logging. Our primary hosting runs on Hetzner data centers in Germany. Whether your processing as a whole meets the GDPR is for you and your data protection officer to assess." },
    { question: "How does Ironum prepare for the EU AI Act?", answer: "Most EU AI Act rules have applied since August 2026; the Digital Omnibus moved the high-risk rules to December 2027 and August 2028. Our setups support the technical side: documentation for risk classification, human-in-the-loop workflows, model documentation, and audit trails for AI-assisted decisions. The legal classification of your system stays with your legal advisers." },
    { question: "Where is my data stored?", answer: "That depends on the deployment you choose. For managed deployments, we use Hetzner data centers in Germany (Nuremberg and Falkenstein). For Azure deployments, we use EU Azure regions. For on-premises deployments, data stays on your own infrastructure. If you choose a commercial model API, data goes to that provider under its terms." },
    { question: "Does Ironum sign a Data Processing Agreement (DPA)?", answer: "Yes. Every Ironum engagement includes a DPA under Art. 28 GDPR and a mutual Non-Disclosure Agreement (NDA) at no additional cost, as standard documents." },
    { question: "Can I get an air-gapped deployment with no internet connection?", answer: "Yes, with open-source models in an on-premises setup. Then the system makes no external API calls and runs inside your network. Updates and model changes are then installed manually. This setup is often asked for in defense, government, and highly regulated industries." },
    { question: "Which certifications apply to the infrastructure?", answer: "Ironum itself holds no certifications such as ISO 27001. Hetzner states that its data centers are ISO 27001 certified. Microsoft lists certifications for Azure, including ISO 27001 and SOC 2. These are the providers' certifications, not ours. For on-premises deployments, your own certifications and requirements apply." },
    { question: "How do you handle data subject access requests (DSAR)?", answer: "Our setups can log processing in a way that lets you find the data linked to a person. When you receive a request, we help you identify, export, correct or delete that data. Answering the request stays your responsibility as the controller." }
  ]} />

  <aside class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 my-10 text-sm text-gray-600">
    <p class="rounded-xl border border-gray-200 bg-gray-50 px-6 py-4"><strong class="font-semibold text-gray-700">Note:</strong> This page is for general information only and does not constitute legal, tax, or data-protection advice. Ironum is a technical service provider, not a law firm. For an assessment of your specific situation, please consult your own qualified legal counsel or data protection officer.</p>
  </aside>
  <FinalCTA />
  <Footer />
</Layout>
